msgid "画像、运行参数与动态状态"
msgstr "Profiles, runtime parameters and dynamic state"

#: ../../../data2/home/huanghaoyu/AgentSociety/agentsociety2/agentsociety/packages/agentsociety2/docs/agents/configuration.rst:120
msgid ""
"``profile`` 描述仿真参与者，例如标识、姓名和背景；``config`` 保存该智能体的静态运行参数。实验配置中的 ``AgentConfig.kwargs`` "
"是编排器创建工作区时使用的输入，具体字段应与所选智能体类匹配。"
msgstr ""
"``profile`` describes a simulation participant, including its identifier, name and background; "
"``config`` stores static runtime parameters for that agent. ``AgentConfig.kwargs`` in the "
"experiment configuration provides input for workspace creation and must match the selected agent "
"class."

#: ../../../data2/home/huanghaoyu/AgentSociety/agentsociety2/agentsociety/packages/agentsociety2/docs/agents/configuration.rst:122
msgid ""
"动态状态在运行后由 workspace 保存。恢复已有实验时，检查 ``AGENT.json`` "
"与状态文件；修改初始配置后需要明确是启动新实验，还是继续原实验，避免误以为恢复操作会重新应用所有初始值。"
msgstr ""
"The workspace saves dynamic state during a run. When resuming an experiment, inspect "
"``AGENT.json`` and state files. After changing initial configuration, decide whether to start a "
"new experiment or resume the existing one; restoration does not necessarily reapply every initial"
" value."

#: ../../../data2/home/huanghaoyu/AgentSociety/agentsociety2/agentsociety/packages/agentsociety2/docs/agents/customization.rst:2
msgid "编写自定义智能体"
msgstr "Writing a custom agent"

#: ../../../data2/home/huanghaoyu/AgentSociety/agentsociety2/agentsociety/packages/agentsociety2/docs/agents/customization.rst:11
msgid "扩展 ``PersonAgent`` 的认知能力，优先使用 Agent Skills（见 :doc:`/agent_skills`）。只有需要完全不同的智能体架构时，才创建自定义智能体类。"
msgstr ""
"When extending ``PersonAgent`` cognitive capabilities, prefer Agent Skills (see "
":doc:`/agent_skills`). Create a custom agent class only when a completely different agent "
"architecture is needed."

msgid ""
"``ask`` 通过 ReAct 循环回答问题。``readonly=True`` 时只暴露查询工具，并限制工作区写入、待办变更和修改环境的工具；``False`` "
"允许使用对应的修改工具。只读问答仍可能记录 trace、更新对话上下文或保存运行时快照。"
msgstr ""
"``ask`` answers questions through the ReAct loop. With ``readonly=True``, only query tools are "
"exposed, restricting workspace writes, TODO changes and state-changing environment tools; "
"``False`` permits the corresponding mutation tools. Read-only questions may still record traces, "
"update conversation context or save runtime snapshots."
